/*  Maps — `a map from … to …`, `a map with (…)`, `the entry for … in …`, `In … becomes`, `has a
    key for`, `has an entry for`, `Remove … from`, `the size of`, and `For each` over the pairs.

    ★ A map is SHARED, as a series is, and two maps are the same map only when they are one map.
      In C it is a pointer to two growable arrays, its keys and its values, kept in the order the
      keys were first added: a key removed closes the gap behind it, and a key added goes on the end
      — the order the interpreter visits them in.

    ★ A lookup gives a voidable — flat when the values are voidable already, never a voidable of a
      voidable.

    ★ Keyed by a number, a text or a fact, or by a record whose fields are keys themselves — two
      records of equal fields are one key. A loop over a map names a `mapping from K to V`: a key
      and its value, as they were when the loop began.
*/

Pull books on collections, and the c-language.
    Bind fact to is-map, given (the text kind):
        Return kind starts with "map from ".
    Done.

    Bind fact to is-mapping, given (the text kind):
        Return kind starts with "mapping from ".
    Done.

    /// How long a map's key is in what follows `map from ` — up to the first ` to ` outside a
    /// record's brackets. No key can hold a map, so no key holds a ` to ` of its own.
    Bind number to key-length, given (the text rest):
        Define depth as 0.
        Define place as 0.
        While place is less than the length of rest, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            Define letter as the characters from place to place of rest.
            If letter is "(", increment depth by 1.
            If letter is ")", decrement depth by 1.
            If depth is 0 and the characters from place to (place + 3) of rest is " to ", return place - 1.
        Done.
        Return place.
    Done.

    /// What follows `map from ` or `mapping from `.
    Bind text to map-rest, given (the text kind):
        If cast is-mapping on (kind), return the characters from 14 to the end of kind.
        Return the characters from 10 to the end of kind.
    Done.

    /// What a map is keyed by.
    Bind text to map-key-kind, given (the text kind):
        Define rest as cast map-rest on (kind).
        Return the characters from 1 to cast key-length on (rest) of rest.
    Done.

    /// What a map holds.
    Bind text to map-value-kind, given (the text kind):
        Define rest as cast map-rest on (kind).
        Return the characters from (cast key-length on (rest) + 5) to the end of rest.
    Done.

    /// Whether a kind can key a map: a number, a text, a fact or bits, a voidable or a union of
    /// keys, or a record of keys.
    Bind fact to is-key-kind, given (the text kind):
        If cast is-scalar on (kind) or kind is "bits", return true.
        If cast is-voidable on (kind), return cast is-key-kind on (cast voidable-inner on (kind)).
        If cast is-union on (kind):
            For each union-case in cast kind-cases on (kind), repeat:
                If cast is-key-kind on (union-case) is false, return false.
            Done.
            Return true.
        Done.
        If cast is-record on (kind) is false, return false.
        For each part in cast record-parts on (kind), repeat:
            If cast is-key-kind on (cast part-kind on (part)) is false, return false.
        Done.
        Return true.
    Done.

    /// What a lookup gives: a voidable of the values, flat when they are voidable already.
    Bind text to looked-up-kind, given (the text kind):
        Define held as cast map-value-kind on (kind).
        If cast is-voidable on (held), return held.
        Return "voidable {held}".
    Done.

    /// A kind as a word fit for a C name.
    Bind text to c-tag, given (the text kind):
        If cast is-scalar on (kind), return kind.
        // An axiom shares a function's struct but not its series, which print it as `<axiom>`.
        If kind starts with "axiom ", return "ax_{cast c-tag on (the characters from 7 to the end of kind)}".
        If kind is "address", return "address".
        Define typed as (cast c-type on (kind)) converted to text.
        If typed ends with "*", return the characters from 1 to (the length of typed - 1) of typed.
        Return typed.
    Done.

    Bind text to map-c-name, given (the text kind):
        Define held as cast map-value-kind on (kind).
        Return "cmap_{cast c-tag on (cast map-key-kind on (kind))}_{cast c-tag on (held)}".
    Done.

    /// The map a mapping comes from.
    Bind text to mapping-map, given (the text kind):
        Return "map from {cast map-key-kind on (kind)} to {cast map-value-kind on (kind)}".
    Done.

    /// Notes a map type the program uses — after what a lookup in it gives, which its helpers return.
    Bind void to register-map unto emitter, given (the text kind):
        Cast one's register-union on (cast looked-up-kind on (kind)).
        If (the entry for kind in one's unions) is void:
            In one's unions, the entry for kind becomes true.
            Insert kind into one's union-order.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// The kind of a written map type, or a failure when it is beyond this compiler.
    Bind text or failure to map-kind-of-type unto emitter, given (the text key-kind, the text held):
        If cast is-key-kind on (key-kind) is false, return a failure (cast not-built on ("a map keyed by a {key-kind}")).
        If held is "void", return a failure (cast not-built on ("a map of void")).
        Define kind as "map from {key-kind} to {held}".
        Cast one's register-map on (kind).
        Return kind.
    Done.

    /// A map's struct, its pairs, and how a map is made, read, changed and written.
    Bind text to c-map-helpers, given (the text kind):
        Define map-c as cast map-c-name on (kind).
        Define key-kind as cast map-key-kind on (kind).
        Define held as cast map-value-kind on (kind).
        Define key-c as cast c-type on (key-kind).
        Define held-c as cast c-type on (held).
        Define looked-c as cast c-type on (cast looked-up-kind on (kind)).
        Define out as a chase.
        Define c-language struct-map-key-form, given (the term map-c-s, the c-language axiom key-c, the c-language axiom held-c),
            as [struct the map-c-s { the key-c* keys; the held-c* vals; int len; int cap; };].
        Insert "{struct-map-key-form on ("{map-c}_s", key-c, held-c)}\n" into out.
        Define c-language typedef-struct-key-form, given (the c-language axiom key-c, the c-language axiom held-c, the term map-c-pair),
            as [typedef struct { the key-c key; the held-c value; } the map-c-pair;].
        Insert "{typedef-struct-key-form on (key-c, held-c, "{map-c}_pair")}\n" into out.
        Define c-language map-c-new-form, given (the term map-c, the term map-c-new),
            as [static the map-c* the map-c-new(void) { the map-c* m = (the map-c*)cufet_arena_alloc(sizeof(the map-c)); m->keys = NULL; m->vals = NULL; m->len = 0; m->cap = 0; return m; }].
        Insert "{map-c-new-form on (map-c, "{map-c}_new")}\n" into out.
        Define c-language map-c-ensure-form, given (the term map-c-ensure, the term map-c, the c-language axiom key-c, the c-language axiom held-c),
            as [static void the map-c-ensure(the map-c* m) { if (m->len >= m->cap) { int nc = m->cap == 0 ? 4 : m->cap * 2; the key-c* nk = (the key-c*)cufet_arena_alloc((size_t)nc * sizeof(the key-c)); the held-c* nv = (the held-c*)cufet_arena_alloc((size_t)nc * sizeof(the held-c)); if (m->len > 0) { memcpy(nk, m->keys, (size_t)m->len * sizeof(the key-c)); memcpy(nv, m->vals, (size_t)m->len * sizeof(the held-c)); } m->keys = nk; m->vals = nv; m->cap = nc; } }].
        Insert "{map-c-ensure-form on ("{map-c}_ensure", map-c, key-c, held-c)}\n" into out.
        Define c-language map-c-index-form, given (the term map-c-index, the term map-c, the c-language axiom key-c, the c-language axiom c-equal),
            as [static int the map-c-index(the map-c* m, the key-c k) { for (int i = 0; i < m->len; i++) if (the c-equal) return i; return -1; }].
        Insert "{map-c-index-form on ("{map-c}_index", map-c, key-c, cast c-equal on (key-kind, [m->keys[i]], [k]))}\n" into out.
        Define c-language map-c-put-form, given (the term map-c-put, the term map-c, the c-language axiom key-c, the c-language axiom held-c, the term map-c-index, the term map-c-ensure),
            as [static void the map-c-put(the map-c* m, the key-c k, the held-c v) { int i = the map-c-index(m, k); if (i >= 0) { m->vals[i] = v; return; } the map-c-ensure(m); m->keys[m->len] = k; m->vals[m->len] = v; m->len++; }].
        Insert "{map-c-put-form on ("{map-c}_put", map-c, key-c, held-c, "{map-c}_index", "{map-c}_ensure")}\n" into out.
        If cast is-voidable on (held):
            Define c-language map-c-get-form, given (the c-language axiom looked-c, the term map-c-get, the term map-c, the c-language axiom key-c, the term map-c-index),
                as [static the looked-c the map-c-get(the map-c* m, the key-c k) { the looked-c r; memset(&r, 0, sizeof r); int i = the map-c-index(m, k); if (i >= 0) r = m->vals[i]; return r; }].
            Insert "{map-c-get-form on (looked-c, "{map-c}_get", map-c, key-c, "{map-c}_index")}\n" into out.
            Define c-language map-c-has-entry-form, given (the term map-c-has-entry, the term map-c, the c-language axiom key-c, the term map-c-index),
                as [static int the map-c-has-entry(the map-c* m, the key-c k) { int i = the map-c-index(m, k); return i >= 0 && m->vals[i].has; }].
            Insert "{map-c-has-entry-form on ("{map-c}_has_entry", map-c, key-c, "{map-c}_index")}\n" into out.
        Done.
        Otherwise:
            Define c-language map-c-get-form-2, given (the c-language axiom looked-c, the term map-c-get, the term map-c, the c-language axiom key-c, the term map-c-index),
                as [static the looked-c the map-c-get(the map-c* m, the key-c k) { the looked-c r; memset(&r, 0, sizeof r); int i = the map-c-index(m, k); if (i >= 0) { r.has = 1; r.value = m->vals[i]; } return r; }].
            Insert "{map-c-get-form-2 on (looked-c, "{map-c}_get", map-c, key-c, "{map-c}_index")}\n" into out.
            Define c-language map-c-has-entry-form-2, given (the term map-c-has-entry, the term map-c, the c-language axiom key-c, the term map-c-index),
                as [static int the map-c-has-entry(the map-c* m, the key-c k) { return the map-c-index(m, k) >= 0; }].
            Insert "{map-c-has-entry-form-2 on ("{map-c}_has_entry", map-c, key-c, "{map-c}_index")}\n" into out.
        Done.
        Define c-language map-c-has-form, given (the term map-c-has, the term map-c, the c-language axiom key-c, the term map-c-index),
            as [static int the map-c-has(the map-c* m, the key-c k) { return the map-c-index(m, k) >= 0; }].
        Insert "{map-c-has-form on ("{map-c}_has", map-c, key-c, "{map-c}_index")}\n" into out.
        Define c-language map-c-remove-form, given (the term map-c-remove, the term map-c, the c-language axiom key-c, the term map-c-index, the c-language axiom held-c),
            as [static void the map-c-remove(the map-c* m, the key-c k, int line) { int i = the map-c-index(m, k); if (i < 0) cufet_raise(cufet_msgf("Key not found in map on line %d.", line)); if (i < m->len - 1) { memmove(&m->keys[i], &m->keys[i + 1], (size_t)(m->len - 1 - i) * sizeof(the key-c)); memmove(&m->vals[i], &m->vals[i + 1], (size_t)(m->len - 1 - i) * sizeof(the held-c)); } m->len--; }].
        Insert "{map-c-remove-form on ("{map-c}_remove", map-c, key-c, "{map-c}_index", held-c)}\n" into out.
        Define c-language map-c-write-form, given (the term map-c-write, the term map-c, the c-language axiom write-call, the c-language axiom write-call-2),
            as [static void the map-c-write(the map-c* m) { fputs("map {", stdout); for (int i = 0; i < m->len; i++) { if (i > 0) fputs(", ", stdout); the write-call; fputs(": ", stdout); the write-call-2; } fputs("}", stdout); }].
        Insert "{map-c-write-form on ("{map-c}_write", map-c, cast write-call on (key-kind, [m->keys[i]]), cast write-call on (held, [m->vals[i]]))}\n" into out.
        Define c-language map-c-pair-write-form, given (the term map-c-pair-write, the term map-c-pair, the c-language axiom write-call, the c-language axiom write-call-2),
            as [static void the map-c-pair-write(the map-c-pair p) { fputs("mapping(", stdout); the write-call; fputs(": ", stdout); the write-call-2; fputs(")", stdout); }].
        Insert "{map-c-pair-write-form on ("{map-c}_pair_write", "{map-c}_pair", cast write-call on (key-kind, [p.key]), cast write-call on (held, [p.value]))}\n" into out.
        Define c-language map-c-pair-eq-form, given (the term map-c-pair-eq, the term map-c-pair, the c-language axiom c-equal, the c-language axiom c-equal-2),
            as [static int the map-c-pair-eq(the map-c-pair a, the map-c-pair b) { return the c-equal && the c-equal-2; }].
        Insert "{map-c-pair-eq-form on ("{map-c}_pair_eq", "{map-c}_pair", cast c-equal on (key-kind, [a.key], [b.key]), cast c-equal on (held, [a.value], [b.value]))}\n\n" into out.
        Return out converted to text.
    Done.

    // ── Expressions ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// The kind a map expression gives, or a failure when it is beyond this compiler.
    Bind text or failure to map-kind-of unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define kind as expression's kind.
        If kind is "MapLiteral":
            If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) is false:
                Define key-kind as cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
                Define held as cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (expression, 2)) or pass the failure off.
                Return cast one's map-kind-of-type on (key-kind, held) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            // `a map with ("a": 1)` names no types — its first entry does.
            Define first-entry as item 1 of (cast field-of on (expression, 3))'s children.
            Define key-kind as cast one's kind-of on (item 1 of first-entry's children) or pass the failure off.
            Define held as cast one's kind-of on (item 2 of first-entry's children) or pass the failure off.
            For each written in (cast field-of on (expression, 3))'s children, repeat:
                Define other-key as cast one's kind-of on (item 1 of written's children) or pass the failure off.
                Define other-held as cast one's kind-of on (item 2 of written's children) or pass the failure off.
                If other-key is not key-kind or other-held is not held:
                    Return a failure (cast not-built on ("a map literal whose entries differ in kind")).
                Done.
            Done.
            Return cast one's map-kind-of-type on (key-kind, held) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        If kind is "MapHasKey" or kind is "MapHasEntry", return "fact".
        If kind is "MapLookup":
            Define looked-in as cast one's kind-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            If cast is-map on (looked-in) is false, return a failure (cast not-built on ("an entry of a {looked-in}")).
            Return cast looked-up-kind on (looked-in).
        Done.
        // `the size of`, `the key of`, `the value of` — a record's fields are for a later slice.
        Define field-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)).
        Define target-kind as cast one's kind-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-map on (target-kind) and field-name is "size", return "number".
        If cast is-mapping on (target-kind):
            If field-name is "key", return cast map-key-kind on (target-kind).
            If field-name is "value", return cast map-value-kind on (target-kind).
        Done.
        If cast object-of on (target-kind) is not "", return cast one's possessive-kind-of on (cast as-possessive on (expression)) or pass the failure off.
        If target-kind is "text" and field-name is "length", return "number".
        If target-kind is "bits" and field-name is "width", return "number".
        If target-kind is "matrix" and (field-name is "rows" or field-name is "columns"), return "number".
        If target-kind is "failure" and cast failure-field-kind on (field-name) is not "", return cast failure-field-kind on (field-name).
        If target-kind is "exception" and field-name is "message", return "text".
        If cast is-record on (target-kind) and cast record-field-kind on (target-kind, field-name) is not "":
            Return cast record-field-kind on (target-kind, field-name).
        Done.
        Return a failure (cast not-built on ("the {field-name} of a {target-kind}")).
    Done.

    /// `the <field> of <object>` as the `<object>'s <field>` it means.
    Bind node to as-possessive, given (the node expression):
        Return cast made on ("PossessiveAccess", a series with (cast field-of on (expression, 2), cast field-of on (expression, 1))).
    Done.

    /// A map expression as C.
    Bind c-language axiom or failure to c-map-of unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define kind as expression's kind.
        If kind is "MapLiteral":
            Define map-kind as cast one's map-kind-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            Define map-c as cast map-c-name on (map-kind).
            Define c-language entry-added, given (the c-language axiom added, the term put, the c-language axiom key, the c-language axiom held),
                as [the added the put(cf_m, the key, the held);].
            Define built as cast no-c.
            For each written in (cast field-of on (expression, 3))'s children, repeat:
                Define key-c as cast one's c-of-as on (item 1 of written's children, cast map-key-kind on (map-kind)) or pass the failure off.
                Define held-c as cast one's c-of-as on (item 2 of written's children, cast map-value-kind on (map-kind)) or pass the failure off.
                The built becomes entry-added on (built, "{map-c}_put", key-c, held-c).
            Done.
            Define c-language map-made, given (the term map-c, the term maker, the c-language axiom built),
                as [({ the map-c* cf_m = the maker(); the built cf_m; })].
            Return map-made on (map-c, "{map-c}_new", built).
        Done.
        If kind is "RecordNamedAccess":
            Define field-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)).
            Define target as cast field-of on (expression, 2).
            Cast one's map-kind-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
            If cast object-of on (cast one's kind-of on (target) or pass the failure off) is not "":
                Return cast one's c-possessive on (cast as-possessive on (expression)) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            Define target-c as cast one's c-of on (target) or pass the failure off.
            Define held-kind as cast one's kind-of on (target) or pass the failure off.
            If held-kind is "text", return cast c-text-length on (target-c).
            If held-kind is "bits":
                Return call-of-one on ("cufet_dec_from_ll", field-read on (target-c, "width")).
            Done.
            If held-kind is "matrix", return cast c-matrix-count on (target-c, field-name).
            If held-kind is "failure", return cast c-failure-field on (target-c, field-name).
            If held-kind is "exception", return target-c.
            If cast is-record on (held-kind), return field-read on (target-c, cast c-name on (field-name)).
            If field-name is "size":
                Define c-language size-held, given (the c-language axiom target), as [cufet_dec_from_ll((the target)->len)].
                Return size-held on (target-c).
            Done.
            If field-name is "key", return field-read on (target-c, "key").
            Return field-read on (target-c, "value").
        Done.
        Define target as cast field-of on (expression, 1).
        Define target-kind as cast one's kind-of on (target) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-map on (target-kind) is false, return a failure (cast not-built on ("an entry of a {target-kind}")).
        Define map-c as cast map-c-name on (target-kind).
        Define target-c as cast one's c-of on (target) or pass the failure off.
        Define key-c as cast one's c-of-as on (cast field-of on (expression, 2), cast map-key-kind on (target-kind)) or pass the failure off.
        // The map first, then the key, as the interpreter works them out — whichever is written first.
        Define sides as a series of c-language axiom with (target-c, key-c).
        Define prefix as cast order-prefix on (a series of node with (target, cast field-of on (expression, 2)), sides).
        If kind is "MapHasKey", return cast in-order on (prefix, call-of-two on ("{map-c}_has", item 1 of sides, item 2 of sides)).
        If kind is "MapHasEntry", return cast in-order on (prefix, call-of-two on ("{map-c}_has_entry", item 1 of sides, item 2 of sides)).
        Return cast in-order on (prefix, call-of-two on ("{map-c}_get", item 1 of sides, item 2 of sides)).
    Done.

    // ── Statements ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// `In <map>, the entry for <key> becomes <value>.`
    Bind void or failure to emit-map-set unto emitter, given (the node statement):
        Define target as cast field-of on (statement, 1).
        Define target-kind as cast one's kind-of on (target) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-map on (target-kind) is false, return a failure (cast not-built on ("an entry of a {target-kind}")).
        Define target-c as cast one's c-of on (target) or pass the failure off.
        Define key-c as cast one's c-of-as on (cast field-of on (statement, 2), cast map-key-kind on (target-kind)) or pass the failure off.
        Define held-c as cast one's c-of-as on (cast field-of on (statement, 3), cast map-value-kind on (target-kind)) or pass the failure off.
        Define sides as a series of c-language axiom with (target-c, key-c, held-c).
        Define prefix as cast order-prefix on (a series of node with (target, cast field-of on (statement, 2), cast field-of on (statement, 3)), sides).
        Cast one's put on (cast in-order-statement on (prefix, done-with on (call-of-three on ("{cast map-c-name on (target-kind)}_put", item 1 of sides, item 2 of sides, item 3 of sides)))).
    Done.

    /// `Remove <key> from <map>.` — refused, as the language does, when the key is not there.
    Bind void or failure to emit-map-remove unto emitter, given (the node statement, the text target-kind):
        Define target-c as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        Define key-c as cast one's c-of-as on (cast field-of on (statement, 2), cast map-key-kind on (target-kind)) or pass the failure off.
        Define sides as a series of c-language axiom with (target-c, key-c).
        Define prefix as cast order-prefix on (a series of node with (cast field-of on (statement, 1), cast field-of on (statement, 2)), sides).
        Cast one's put on (cast in-order-statement on (prefix, done-with on (call-at-line on ("{cast map-c-name on (target-kind)}_remove", item 1 of sides, item 2 of sides, cast line-number on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)))))).
    Done.

    /// `For each <name> in <map>, repeat:` — over the pairs as they were when it began. A key added
    /// or removed while it runs is refused before the next pass, as the interpreter does — and not
    /// on the way out, which a series loop also checks.
    Bind void or failure to emit-map-for-each unto emitter, given (the node statement, the text held):
        Define named as cast field-of on (statement, 1).
        Define name as "it".
        If cast is-nothing on (named) is false, the name becomes cast unquoted on (named).
        Define over as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
        Define map-c as cast map-c-name on (held).
        Define key-c as cast c-type on (cast map-key-kind on (held)).
        Define held-c as cast c-type on (cast map-value-kind on (held)).
        Define label as "The map".
        If over's kind is "VariableReference", the label becomes "'{cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (over, 1))}'".
        Define map-value as cast one's c-of on (over) or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's put on ([{]).
        Define kept as a map from text to text.
        For each pair in one's kinds, repeat:
            In kept, the entry for the key of pair becomes the value of pair.
        Done.
        Define outer as one's indent.
        The one's indent becomes outer joined to "    ".
        Define c-language map-each-map-form, given (the term map-c, the c-language axiom map-value),
            as [the map-c* cf_each = the map-value;].
        Cast one's put on (map-each-map-form on (map-c, map-value)).
        Cast one's put on ([int cf_each_n = cf_each->len;]).
        Define c-language key-keys-key-form, given (the c-language axiom key-c),
            as [the key-c* cf_keys = (the key-c*)cufet_arena_alloc((size_t)(cf_each_n + 1) * sizeof(the key-c));].
        Cast one's put on (key-keys-key-form on (key-c)).
        Define c-language held-vals-held-form, given (the c-language axiom held-c),
            as [the held-c* cf_vals = (the held-c*)cufet_arena_alloc((size_t)(cf_each_n + 1) * sizeof(the held-c));].
        Cast one's put on (held-vals-held-form on (held-c)).
        Define c-language each-memcpy-keys-form, given (the c-language axiom key-c, the c-language axiom held-c),
            as [if (cf_each_n > 0) { memcpy(cf_keys, cf_each->keys, (size_t)cf_each_n * sizeof(the key-c)); memcpy(cf_vals, cf_each->vals, (size_t)cf_each_n * sizeof(the held-c)); }].
        Cast one's put on (each-memcpy-keys-form on (key-c, held-c)).
        Cast one's put on ([for (int cf_i = 0; cf_i < cf_each_n; cf_i++) {]).
        Define mapping-kind as "mapping from {cast map-key-kind on (held)} to {cast map-value-kind on (held)}".
        In one's kinds, the entry for name becomes mapping-kind.
        Cast one's declared-here on (name).
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%{name}" becomes mapping-kind.
        In one's kinds, the entry for "@{name}" becomes "".
        The one's indent becomes outer joined to "        ".
        Define c-language each-len-each-form, given (the text message),
            as [if (cf_each->len != cf_each_n) cufet_raise(cufet_msgf(the message));].
        Cast one's put on (each-len-each-form on ("{label} was modified during a for-each loop on line {(cast field-of on (statement, 4))'s word} — collect into a separate series, or use a While loop if you need to change it while looping.")).
        Define c-language map-pair-name-form, given (the term map-c-pair, the term c-name),
            as [the map-c-pair the c-name = { cf_keys[cf_i], cf_vals[cf_i] };].
        Cast one's put on (map-pair-name-form on ("{map-c}_pair", cast c-name on (name))).
        The one's indent becomes outer joined to "    ".
        Define loop-kept as cast one's entering-loop.
        Cast one's emit-block on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)) or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's leaving-loop on (loop-kept).
        Cast one's put on ([}]).
        The one's indent becomes outer.
        The one's kinds becomes kept.
        Cast one's put on ([}]).
    Done.
Done.
